WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.040
Maruo

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:04.020
Bro's got match point!

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:27.340
Game, set, and match.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:30.300
Winner: Maruo. Score: 6-2.

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:31.550
<i>Yes!</i>

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:34.050
<i>I won...</i>

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:37.150
<i>I won with my own skill!</i>

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:08.520
Kanagawa Junior 
Tennis Tournament Arena

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:11.090
Court 6, Maruo Eiichiro.

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:12.560
I won, 6-2.

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:16.230
All right, you're finished 
for the day, Maruo-kun.

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:17.440
Good work!

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:19.910
And I'm Takasaki Natsu, from Court 1.

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:21.440
I won, 6-0!

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:22.360
Nat-chan.

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:25.830
You beat Miyagawa-kun, 6-2?

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:27.100
That's amazing!

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:30.670
But getting there was much tougher 
than the score makes it seem.

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:34.340
Regardless, we're both one step 
closer to the All-Japan Junior!

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:35.310
Yeah.

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:39.140
Huh? You don't seem as happy 
as I thought you'd be.

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:42.220
Huh? No, it's not that, but...

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:43.160
"But"?

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:46.240
Somehow... Unlike how it's been in the past,

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:48.700
it was a real struggle to win.

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:51.970
I guess it showed me how 
intense a real match can be.

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:56.230
So you had <i>that</i> type of match.

00:02:56.490 --> 00:02:58.410
I can understand how that feels.

00:02:58.410 --> 00:02:59.250
Huh?

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:02.490
But you'll probably have more 
matches like that in the future.

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:04.000
The more you win.

00:03:04.970 --> 00:03:06.240
<i>That's right...</i>

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:09.530
<i>Nat-chan's experienced this lots of times.</i>

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:13.920
It may feel that way to you now 
since the match just ended,

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:15.730
but you'll understand soon

00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:19.170
that the truly fun matches are 
the ones that feel that way.

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:27.340
<i>I was able to defeat Miyagawa-kun.</i>

00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:30.230
<i>In retrospect, it was by a large deficit.</i>

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:31.980
Thoughts on Today

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:35.910
<i>From the beginning of the match, 
I felt like I was ahead in terms of skill,</i>

00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:38.060
<i>but I couldn't relax for even a second.</i>

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:42.060
<i>That prickling fear wouldn't go away...</i>

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:44.120
<i>It's probably because I knew</i>

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:46.280
<i>Miyagawa-kun's future was 
riding on this match.</i>

00:03:46.990 --> 00:03:48.680
<i>This wasn't a match he could</i>

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:50.850
<i>afford to lose if he wanted to move forward.</i>

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:56.360
<i>So today's match may have 
changed Miyagawa-kun's whole life.</i>

00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:59.170
<i>My life may have changed, as well.</i>

00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:02.840
<i>This is probably what a 
true match feels like.</i>

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:06.260
<i>I'm not exactly sure about 
what Nat-chan was saying,</i>

00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:10.770
<i>but I wonder if I'm really going to 
have a lot more matches like this.</i>

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:13.270
<i>In any case,</i>

00:04:13.270 --> 00:04:17.270
Kanagawa Junior Tennis Tournament VS Miyagawa Takuya

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:16.870
<i>I doubt I'll ever forget today's match.</i>

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:24.270
Baffled by Intuition

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:27.780
Yes!

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:29.300
Game, set, and match.

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:31.850
Winner: Maruo. Score: 6-1.

00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:37.200
Game, set, and match.

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:40.040
Winner: Maruo. Score: 6-0.

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:42.970
He made it to the top four unseeded?

00:04:42.970 --> 00:04:45.800
That match against Miyagawa 
wasn't a fluke after all.

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:47.390
With this tournament,

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:50.180
Maruo's definitely made a name
for himself in Kanagawa.

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:52.380
He's completely different from last year.

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:53.290
No kidding!

00:04:53.590 --> 00:04:57.260
He was completely different 
from what you told me!

00:04:57.260 --> 00:04:58.690
That's not my fault.

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:01.460
If you wanna complain, take it up with 
Maruo, the one who got stronger.

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:06.450
In tomorrow's semifinals, 
which do you think will move up?

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:08.200
The second seed, Mogami, or Maruo-san?

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:10.500
It doesn't matter which.

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:19.820
<i>The Kanagawa Junior Circuit U-12 
Boys' Champion is Egawa Takuma-kun.</i>

00:05:20.190 --> 00:05:22.750
<i>The runner-up is Araya Hiroshi-kun.</i>

00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:26.270
Egawa Takuma-kun is really something special.

00:05:26.270 --> 00:05:29.160
Players like him only come 
along once every ten years.

00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:32.340
<i>Damn, that's ten straight losses.</i>

00:05:32.340 --> 00:05:33.450
<i>This is no joke.</i>

00:05:33.450 --> 00:05:35.560
<i>I'm not going to be second 
for the rest of my life!</i>

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:37.690
<i>I'm going pro, too!</i>

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:43.300
Game, set.

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:45.530
Winner: Egawa Takuma.

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:49.700
Score: 4-6, 7-5, 7-5.

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:56.790
<i>I don't want the title of 
Kanagawa's second best anymore.</i>

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:58.870
<i>I'm going to stand at the top.</i>

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:04.630
<i>I can see how he was able to beat Miyagawa!</i>

00:06:07.630 --> 00:06:08.470
<i>Cross!</i>

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:12.570
Yes!

00:06:12.570 --> 00:06:14.010
Game, set, and match.

00:06:14.010 --> 00:06:17.560
Winner: Maruo. Score 6-3, 6-2.

00:06:19.130 --> 00:06:21.310
An unseeded player's going to the final!

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:23.420
It's completely unexpected.

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:25.750
Maruo-kun, that was incredible!

00:06:25.750 --> 00:06:29.080
Hey, hey, I can't believe you 
actually made it to the final!

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:30.090
Yeah.

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:33.280
To think, just last year, you 
were losing in the third round!

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:36.690
I think being able to defeat 
Miyagawa-kun had a huge impact.

00:06:37.340 --> 00:06:40.790
<i>I feel like something's majorly
changed since that match.</i>

00:06:40.790 --> 00:06:44.290
Just to let you know, this is 
all according to plan thus far.

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:45.800
Coach Aoi.

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:48.300
As expected, your final match is against Araya.

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:52.430
Game, set, and match.

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:56.060
Winner: Araya. Score: 6-2, 6-1.

00:06:56.260 --> 00:06:57.810
Yeah!

00:06:57.810 --> 00:06:59.520
Which means...

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:02.380
You know better than 
anyone else that it won't

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:04.830
go as it has in the past, right?

00:07:04.830 --> 00:07:06.570
Yes. He's a strong opponent.

00:07:06.930 --> 00:07:10.190
He's a regular at the All-Japan Junior, 
and he's also aiming to go pro.

00:07:10.190 --> 00:07:12.860
In other words, he's not only 
someone of a higher rank

00:07:12.860 --> 00:07:14.330
whom you have to surpass by summer,

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:16.830
but he's also someone 
who's defeated you before.

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:19.830
However, I predict that you can win.

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:23.400
Anything is possible.

00:07:25.140 --> 00:07:26.760
Uh, sorry,

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:30.120
but did you have to end that thought 
on such a discouraging note?

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:33.550
What can I say? I'm telling it like it is.

00:07:34.230 --> 00:07:37.420
If you have the time to be worried, 
then let's get to practicing.

00:07:37.420 --> 00:07:38.350
Okay!

00:07:40.910 --> 00:07:43.230
Oh, he's at it!

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:44.730
Oh, Nat-chan.

00:07:45.630 --> 00:07:47.380
You're in the final, too, huh?

00:07:47.380 --> 00:07:48.980
Let's do our best tomorrow, okay?

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:49.920
Yeah.

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:52.150
It'd be great if we could both win together.

00:07:52.150 --> 00:07:53.810
Aoi-kun, do you have a moment?

00:07:53.810 --> 00:07:56.120
What is it, Coach Sakakibara?

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:58.640
If you're asking me out on a date, 
we can talk later in private...

00:07:58.640 --> 00:07:59.370
I'm not!

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:02.660
You're a hot topic among the girls now.

00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:04.630
They're psyched that an 
unseeded player is in the final!

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:07.290
Don't put that kind of pressure on me!

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:11.040
My rank is low, so if I don't win 
this prefectural tournament,

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:13.010
I can't place in the top seeds.

00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:15.740
Oh, yeah... If you stay unseeded,

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:18.390
you'll end up facing a seeded player sooner.

00:08:18.830 --> 00:08:21.200
To qualify for the All-Japan Junior,

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:24.220
I have to get past the second 
round in the Kanto Junior,

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:27.440
so I'd have the upper hand
if I were a seeded player.

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:29.890
All right, Maruo and Natsu.

00:08:29.890 --> 00:08:30.690
Yeah?

00:08:30.690 --> 00:08:33.240
The two of you play against each other.

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:34.250
What?!

00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:38.080
Why am I playing against 
Nat-chan... against a girl?

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:41.050
I'm not telling you to do it just for fun.

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:45.580
For Natsu, this'll help prepare her for
Shimizu Aki in the All-Japan Junior.

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:47.170
Shimizu-san?

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:50.740
Right now, you barely have any 
rivals in the Kanto region,

00:08:50.740 --> 00:08:54.300
so you haven't been able to play 
against a high-level player, right?

00:08:54.640 --> 00:08:56.970
Plus, the way Maruo-kun uses control is

00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:59.530
similar to how Shimizu-san plays tennis.

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:04.180
And for Maruo, to put it simply, 
this is mental training.

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:07.800
There are times I watch you 
play during matches and

00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:09.940
wish you could play more like Natsu.

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:12.200
What does that mean?

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:15.950
You two are true contrasts to one another.

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:18.440
If Maruo were the logical type,

00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:20.330
Natsu would be the intuitive type.

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:23.110
Of course, both of those 
characteristics are fantastic,

00:09:23.110 --> 00:09:25.210
so it's not like we want you to change them.

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:28.600
But watching you, there are times when I think

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:33.170
you'd benefit from learning how 
to play tennis more intuitively.

00:09:33.540 --> 00:09:34.550
Oh...

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:37.630
Instead of picking apart the details, just try it.

00:09:37.940 --> 00:09:40.280
Doesn't it sound fun? Come on.

00:09:40.280 --> 00:09:42.640
But I understand what you mean.

00:09:42.990 --> 00:09:47.650
I was able to move very 
intuitively in Florida, just once.

00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:50.920
And I played a surprisingly 
good match because of it.

00:09:53.270 --> 00:09:57.280
I really do wish I could play 
like that intentionally.

00:09:57.280 --> 00:09:58.070
Oh?

00:09:58.270 --> 00:10:01.780
Um, will this match be played like usual?

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:03.230
That's right.

00:10:03.230 --> 00:10:06.330
It's just one set, but treat 
it like a regular match.

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:09.330
Wait a second, Ei-chan... 
What's that supposed to mean?

00:10:09.620 --> 00:10:11.910
Are you saying that a boy playing seriously

00:10:11.910 --> 00:10:13.950
against a girl would be unfair?

00:10:13.950 --> 00:10:15.690
N-No!

00:10:15.690 --> 00:10:18.930
I've never played a match against a girl, 
so I don't know how it works!

00:10:19.250 --> 00:10:21.620
Natsu, you don't have to 
worry about it if you lose,

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:24.400
so just prioritize watching how Maruo plays.

00:10:24.400 --> 00:10:28.440
Hey! Coach Aoi, you're assuming 
I'm going to lose, too?

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:30.360
That's not right.

00:10:30.360 --> 00:10:32.690
You're not even that much taller!

00:10:33.080 --> 00:10:36.430
And I watch Ei-chan every day, 
so I know exactly how he plays.

00:10:36.430 --> 00:10:39.820
If you think you're gonna 
win so easily, think again!

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:42.320
<i>Her reasoning is all over the place...</i>

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:43.550
Okay, fine!

00:10:43.550 --> 00:10:44.460
So which side?

00:10:44.460 --> 00:10:46.430
Huh? Oh... Upper, then.

00:10:46.850 --> 00:10:49.120
I'm lower. It's my serve.

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:51.830
You're both warmed up, right?

00:10:55.090 --> 00:10:56.490
Do your best.

00:10:56.490 --> 00:10:57.590
O-Okay.

00:10:57.870 --> 00:11:00.360
All right, one-set match. Play!

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:03.600
<i>I wonder what Nat-chan's serve is like...</i>

00:11:06.530 --> 00:11:07.740
15-love.

00:11:07.740 --> 00:11:09.020
See? Ace.

00:11:09.020 --> 00:11:10.970
<i>I-It's faster than I expected!</i>

00:11:10.970 --> 00:11:13.080
Stop spacing out!

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:15.270
Just because you're ranked in Japan's top class

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:17.280
doesn't mean you're allowed to lose to a girl.

00:11:17.620 --> 00:11:18.860
It could happen!

00:11:18.860 --> 00:11:19.750
<i>This is bad!</i>

00:11:19.750 --> 00:11:21.360
<i>I can't get myself to focus!</i>

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:24.940
<i>Playing like this is rude to Nat-chan 
and a waste of a practice!</i>

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:27.810
<i>Speaking of, Mike once 
mentioned that the process</i>

00:11:27.810 --> 00:11:31.120
<i>of falling in love and being in battle 
are the opposite of each other.</i>

00:11:32.660 --> 00:11:33.850
<i>All right.</i>

00:11:33.850 --> 00:11:36.880
<i>I'll imagine that I'm fighting 
Nabae-kun right now.</i>

00:11:37.140 --> 00:11:40.390
<i>My opponent right now isn't a girl, 
it's a top-class male player!</i>

00:11:40.390 --> 00:11:42.320
<i>A big hurdle I have to overcome.</i>

00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:44.140
<i>A powerful opponent I have to defeat.</i>

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:47.260
<i>The number one player in 
the country, Nabae Yu!</i>

00:11:48.700 --> 00:11:50.310
<i>As if I could think that!</i>

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:51.810
30-love.

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:55.230
<i>Is it really okay for me to be doing this?</i>

00:11:56.880 --> 00:11:57.820
4-0!

00:11:57.820 --> 00:12:00.020
Araya-san, you're being way too intense!

00:12:00.430 --> 00:12:02.180
Knowing who it is I'm facing, I don't want

00:12:02.180 --> 00:12:04.070
to let my guard down until the end.

00:12:04.070 --> 00:12:07.450
More importantly, you're not playing 
adequately as Maruo's proxy.

00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:10.980
Come at me!

00:12:18.370 --> 00:12:21.620
<i>I can't possibly imagine 
Nat-chan as Nabae-kun.</i>

00:12:22.140 --> 00:12:24.230
<i>I'll just do what Coach Aoi told me to do</i>

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:27.050
<i>and take in Nat-chan's tennis style.</i>

00:12:27.050 --> 00:12:29.810
<i>I want to be able to play more intuitively.</i>

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:31.760
<i>A fast wide serve!</i>

00:12:32.110 --> 00:12:34.310
<i>If I calm down, I can return it!</i>

00:12:34.950 --> 00:12:35.750
<i>What?!</i>

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:38.650
<i>She created an open court with that wide serve,</i>

00:12:38.650 --> 00:12:40.860
<i>so why did she hit it straight?</i>

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:42.620
<i>A slow ball, no less!</i>

00:12:42.620 --> 00:12:43.820
<i>Then I'll go...</i>

00:12:43.820 --> 00:12:44.950
<i>Deep crosscourt!</i>

00:12:46.770 --> 00:12:48.340
<i>She went for a power hit here?!</i>

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:51.470
Out. 40-love.

00:12:51.470 --> 00:12:52.670
<i>What?!</i>

00:12:52.670 --> 00:12:54.760
<i>Why would she go for such a hard hit now?</i>

00:12:54.760 --> 00:12:57.010
<i>If she'd hit a hard shot to 
that open court earlier,</i>

00:12:57.010 --> 00:12:59.100
<i>it would've been easier for her to win the point.</i>

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:00.990
<i>Fast!</i>

00:13:00.990 --> 00:13:02.720
<i>Are they going to get even faster?</i>

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:04.270
<i>She's confident in where she aims, too.</i>

00:13:04.270 --> 00:13:05.510
<i>I need to be careful.</i>

00:13:05.850 --> 00:13:07.970
<i>But the second serve will be my chance.</i>

00:13:10.280 --> 00:13:12.270
<i>This time I'll go straight 
from the return to...</i>

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:12.770
<i>What?!</i>

00:13:13.790 --> 00:13:14.600
<i>Forward?!</i>

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:19.690
Game: Natsu. 1-0.

00:13:18.660 --> 00:13:19.690
Yeah!

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:22.320
<i>Th-That was definitely weird just now!</i>

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:25.360
<i>Coming to the net on a second serve, 
against a male opponent...</i>

00:13:25.360 --> 00:13:27.450
<i>No matter how I look at it, that's reckless!</i>

00:13:27.690 --> 00:13:30.440
<i>But I missed my timing because of it,</i>

00:13:30.440 --> 00:13:31.950
<i>so is this her strategy?</i>

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:34.370
<i>Or am I overthinking it?</i>

00:13:35.350 --> 00:13:37.270
<i>I have no idea!</i>

00:13:38.230 --> 00:13:41.710
<i>But at the very least, I have to hold serve.</i>

00:13:42.450 --> 00:13:44.260
<i>I'll just go for it and...</i>

00:13:45.470 --> 00:13:46.440
So fast!

00:13:46.840 --> 00:13:50.900
Whoa, whoa, that was brutal!
And you call yourself a man?

00:13:50.900 --> 00:13:53.470
You're the one who told 
me to take it seriously!

00:13:53.470 --> 00:13:55.780
Natsu, the key to speed is getting used to it.

00:13:55.780 --> 00:13:57.470
If you can get used to a boy's speed,

00:13:57.470 --> 00:13:59.590
it'll be easier for you to 
deal with a girl's serve.

00:13:59.590 --> 00:14:00.360
Right!

00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:05.160
<i>It went in, and she was 
still able to make contact...</i>

00:14:09.420 --> 00:14:11.280
Game: Maruo. 1-all.

00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:14.630
<i>I didn't know Ei-chan's serves 
were this impressive.</i>

00:14:14.630 --> 00:14:16.290
<i>But I'll return it next time.</i>

00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:19.670
<i>A deep slice.</i>

00:14:20.120 --> 00:14:23.290
<i>Nat-chan will probably use the time it 
takes for me to get there, and move up...</i>

00:14:23.290 --> 00:14:24.670
<i>She isn't?!</i>

00:14:25.980 --> 00:14:26.920
<i>No! Too shallow!</i>

00:14:27.890 --> 00:14:29.710
<i>But she isn't going in for the score.</i>

00:14:29.710 --> 00:14:32.180
<i>Is running back and forth a weak point?</i>

00:14:32.180 --> 00:14:35.100
<i>If that's the case, I'll hit it deep and run up!</i>

00:14:41.790 --> 00:14:43.770
Game: Maruo. 2-1.

00:14:44.340 --> 00:14:46.780
You've done great so far, Natsu.

00:14:47.070 --> 00:14:48.760
But from here, Maruo-kun's

00:14:48.760 --> 00:14:51.950
plan of attack is to make you run 
back and forth, so be aware.

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:52.530
Okay.

00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:56.220
Your timing has been off by a beat.

00:14:56.220 --> 00:14:58.830
If Natsu's footwork was 
that of a male player's,

00:14:58.830 --> 00:15:00.690
you'd definitely be destroyed.

00:15:00.690 --> 00:15:04.040
That's because I have no 
idea what she's thinking...

00:15:04.040 --> 00:15:07.050
I told you. Natsu plays intuitively.

00:15:07.440 --> 00:15:10.050
That's what's amazing about her.

00:15:10.360 --> 00:15:12.710
You won't be able to figure 
it out by thinking about it.

00:15:12.710 --> 00:15:13.990
So just watch with your eyes,

00:15:13.990 --> 00:15:17.070
feel it with your body, 
and listen to your instincts.

00:15:17.690 --> 00:15:20.670
<i>Watch, feel, and obey.</i>

00:15:22.290 --> 00:15:26.560
<i>That's what I felt in Florida that time...</i>

00:15:28.030 --> 00:15:31.240
Don't you think it's kinda 
similar to being in love?

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:32.780
H-Huh?

00:15:33.660 --> 00:15:36.490
<i>Watch, feel, obey...</i>

00:15:40.070 --> 00:15:42.080
<i>She returned one!</i>

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:44.120
<i>Nat-chan really is amazing.</i>

00:15:44.120 --> 00:15:46.590
<i>As usual, I can't tell how she'll respond.</i>

00:15:48.010 --> 00:15:51.840
<i>So instead of guessing, I'll just focus 
on hitting a mix of short and deep.</i>

00:15:53.690 --> 00:15:55.970
<i>Ei-chan's reactions are getting faster.</i>

00:15:55.970 --> 00:15:57.540
<i>And that's not all.</i>

00:15:57.540 --> 00:16:00.430
<i>All of his shots are intended to
keep me running back and forth.</i>

00:16:00.430 --> 00:16:02.480
<i>He's controlling even the 
moves I've yet to make!</i>

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:05.570
<i>It's like he's figuring me out more and more.</i>

00:16:06.270 --> 00:16:07.230
<i>Incredible!</i>

00:16:13.990 --> 00:16:15.980
So this is what we're working with.

00:16:15.980 --> 00:16:16.990
Yeah.

00:16:21.330 --> 00:16:25.490
Game, set. Winner: Maruo. Score: 6-1.

00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:30.340
Natsu
Maruo

00:16:25.490 --> 00:16:27.470
Good job, both of you.

00:16:27.470 --> 00:16:30.340
That's it for today. Rest up for tomorrow.

00:16:30.340 --> 00:16:32.120
<i>That was really tiring.</i>

00:16:32.120 --> 00:16:33.840
<i>Not for my body, but for my mind...</i>

00:16:37.850 --> 00:16:40.850
That was fun! Let's do it again sometime.

00:16:42.220 --> 00:16:44.100
It was a great experience.

00:16:44.950 --> 00:16:49.170
<i>But I feel like what I learned in this 
match will be useful to me someday!</i>

00:16:59.630 --> 00:17:00.690
6-0.

00:17:00.690 --> 00:17:02.930
Come on, we're moving on to the second set.

00:17:02.930 --> 00:17:04.910
Tomorrow's the final!

00:17:04.910 --> 00:17:06.500
Let's wrap this up!

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:10.750
This is nothing compared to 
how much our club practices!

00:17:11.020 --> 00:17:13.570
That's because it's you, Araya-san.

00:17:13.570 --> 00:17:16.940
I want you to win the final 
tomorrow, no matter what.

00:17:17.570 --> 00:17:19.140
You don't need to tell me that.

00:17:19.450 --> 00:17:22.510
I want you to show everyone 
how strong our club really is.

00:17:24.270 --> 00:17:27.270
Call it a day, Araya. I want to talk to you.

00:17:29.420 --> 00:17:32.650
I'm aware that you want to go pro 
after you graduate high school.

00:17:33.180 --> 00:17:34.810
Your schedule up to that point

00:17:34.810 --> 00:17:36.910
will be determined by how you 
do in the All-Japan Junior.

00:17:37.650 --> 00:17:38.480
Right.

00:17:39.040 --> 00:17:41.040
You've done a great job to get here.

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:45.690
From here on, our club will be fully dedicated

00:17:45.690 --> 00:17:48.420
to supporting your path toward going pro.

00:17:48.970 --> 00:17:50.420
We can do that for you

00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:53.210
because you made it through 
this difficult program

00:17:53.210 --> 00:17:55.170
designed for players who want to go pro.

00:17:55.820 --> 00:17:58.430
There aren't many who can get to this point.

00:17:58.790 --> 00:18:02.780
Only those who have gifted bodies and 
train them to the fullest can get here.

00:18:05.430 --> 00:18:06.770
Use your entire body for more power!

00:18:09.920 --> 00:18:11.780
Hey, what's wrong? Stand up!

00:18:14.810 --> 00:18:16.960
If you can't keep up, this is it for you.

00:18:19.380 --> 00:18:21.200
Hey, wait a second!

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:23.980
Don't give up! You can keep going, can't you?

00:18:23.980 --> 00:18:25.450
Let go of me.

00:18:25.850 --> 00:18:27.520
You're lucky

00:18:27.990 --> 00:18:29.710
to have the physique you do.

00:18:30.190 --> 00:18:33.440
It's impossible for me.

00:18:35.990 --> 00:18:38.230
How long are you gonna rest, Araya?

00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:43.910
Faster!

00:18:44.280 --> 00:18:46.730
It's about how fast you can
reach your top speed!

00:18:47.300 --> 00:18:49.410
Move quickly and shoot hard!

00:18:49.410 --> 00:18:51.010
That's what the future of tennis is!

00:18:52.960 --> 00:18:54.040
Kawai!

00:18:54.440 --> 00:18:55.480
What are you doing, Araya?!

00:18:55.960 --> 00:18:57.220
Don't just stop!

00:18:57.220 --> 00:18:58.730
But Kawai's...

00:18:58.730 --> 00:19:00.740
That's not your job.

00:19:00.740 --> 00:19:01.870
You need to run!

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:13.130
Everyone here is your rival.

00:19:13.580 --> 00:19:15.580
Think only about coming out on top.

00:19:21.110 --> 00:19:23.890
Hey, Araya! Sorry about earlier.

00:19:30.250 --> 00:19:33.250
Is it true that you're quitting?

00:19:34.090 --> 00:19:35.650
Oh, you heard?

00:19:36.860 --> 00:19:39.240
I decided to give up on going pro.

00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:45.670
No matter what I do, I just can't 
move as fast as you or hit as hard.

00:19:46.600 --> 00:19:48.950
It's about time I came to terms with it.

00:19:50.410 --> 00:19:53.360
But I love tennis, so I'll continue playing...

00:19:54.170 --> 00:19:55.240
So...

00:19:56.170 --> 00:19:57.830
You have to do your best.

00:19:58.130 --> 00:20:00.160
You're our hope.

00:20:02.810 --> 00:20:07.100
We're planning to create the 
ideal environment for you.

00:20:07.100 --> 00:20:09.160
If there's anything you need, let us know.

00:20:09.160 --> 00:20:10.680
Thank you.

00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:17.730
Kanawaga Junior 
Tennis Tournament Arena

00:20:19.990 --> 00:20:23.740
Outdoor                Outdoor

00:20:19.990 --> 00:20:23.740
Today's Matches

00:20:19.990 --> 00:20:23.740
Araya Hiroshi           Takasaki Natsu
vs                                   vs
Maruo Eiichiro                 Sakurai Rei

00:20:34.990 --> 00:20:37.210
<i>Ever since I was a kid, the path to going pro</i>

00:20:37.210 --> 00:20:40.110
<i>has been my goal, and I've left 
my friends behind to reach it.</i>

00:20:40.630 --> 00:20:44.800
<i>For the club, for my friends, 
and more than anything, for myself...</i>

00:20:47.410 --> 00:20:51.410
<i>As a future pro player, I won't lose to you!</i>

00:21:02.010 --> 00:21:04.030
<i>I have more than enough data on Araya-kun.</i>

00:21:04.660 --> 00:21:05.870
<i>He's left-handed.</i>

00:21:05.870 --> 00:21:08.760
<i>He's a baseliner who attacks 
with speed and power.</i>

00:21:09.130 --> 00:21:11.520
<i>His counter shots are powerful.</i>

00:21:11.520 --> 00:21:16.610
Take Down Araya File
1. Aim for his weak point: his slow start.
2. Take your time during points and play at your own pace.
3. Contest of endurance.
4. It's important to concede points sometimes.
Especially with Araya-kun who has both speed and power on his side,
 it's normal to lose from time to time.
5. Avoid his fast-paced tempo and surprise him.

00:21:11.830 --> 00:21:13.790
<i>He's impatient and short-tempered,</i>

00:21:13.800 --> 00:21:16.520
<i>but in our last match, he adjusted his play in the end.</i>

00:21:16.910 --> 00:21:19.960
<i>He has a habit of dropping his 
shoulder after a cross counter.</i>

00:21:20.430 --> 00:21:23.300
<i>For everything else, I just 
have to play him and find out.</i>

00:21:24.620 --> 00:21:26.300
<i>Today's the day...</i>

00:21:30.640 --> 00:21:32.260
Go in!

00:21:33.680 --> 00:21:35.410
<i>...I'll repay him for that.</i>

00:21:36.640 --> 00:21:37.690
Serve.

00:21:37.690 --> 00:21:39.270
Then I'll be on this side.

00:21:41.090 --> 00:21:42.580
Good luck.

00:21:43.860 --> 00:21:45.120
Good luck.

00:21:46.270 --> 00:21:47.700
<i>This feeling...</i>

00:21:47.700 --> 00:21:52.430
<i>It's the same sensation of prickling fear 
that I felt with Miyagawa-kun.</i>

00:21:53.160 --> 00:21:55.610
<i>The reason I didn't feel this way last year</i>

00:21:55.610 --> 00:21:58.420
<i>is probably because I wasn't 
fully focused on going pro.</i>

00:21:58.880 --> 00:22:00.920
<i>I have to overcome this first.</i>

00:22:01.330 --> 00:22:03.210
<i>My desire won't lose to his!</i>

00:22:05.120 --> 00:22:08.550
<i>Last year, he went after me before 
I could get my engine started,</i>

00:22:08.900 --> 00:22:11.350
<i>but I won't be playing that way anymore.</i>

00:22:11.650 --> 00:22:13.240
<i>I'm going all-in from the start!</i>

00:22:13.780 --> 00:22:15.970
<i>Even my tendency to rush the game</i>

00:22:15.970 --> 00:22:17.980
<i>can be turned into a weapon if I control it.</i>

00:22:18.330 --> 00:22:21.900
<i>You were the one who taught me that.</i>

00:22:21.900 --> 00:22:24.040
Best-of-three-set match.

00:22:24.040 --> 00:22:25.710
Araya to serve.

00:22:30.760 --> 00:22:31.670
<i>Here I come!</i>

00:24:00.020 --> 00:24:25.040
Next Time

00:24:00.620 --> 00:24:03.560
All right! I'm giving it everything from the start!

00:24:03.560 --> 00:24:05.590
He has even more power than last year!

00:24:05.590 --> 00:24:08.210
You've gotten a lot stronger, haven't you?!

00:24:08.210 --> 00:24:10.640
His speed and the volume 
of his voice have increased,

00:24:10.640 --> 00:24:12.220
yet he looks calm.

00:24:12.720 --> 00:24:17.220
Item 1 of my Take Down Araya File from
last year, his slow start, has been fixed!

00:24:17.220 --> 00:24:21.380
I'll show you how different the 
two of us are, right here and now!

00:24:21.380 --> 00:24:23.120
Next time on <i>Baby Steps</i>,

00:24:21.540 --> 00:24:25.040
Start with a Roar

00:24:23.120 --> 00:24:24.520
"Start with a Roar."

00:24:25.210 --> 00:24:30.300
End
